  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="df521b23-11ef-53f3-9f04-7f3360441ce2" activityNameId="9d4fcc6d-93fb-58ab-be2d-b217d6f3fe97" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production RU, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production RU, at long-distance pipeline
In 2019 100% of the imported Russian natural gas to DE was imported by pipeline and 0% as LNG. An average distance of 4860 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Russian Federation, of which are 410 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 11700 km.;
5bf64358-ff40-3ab3-b6e9-415948badd4c
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Russian natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location:  The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2019.
Production volume: none
Sampling: Literature. Online calculators for distances.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5bf64358-ff40-3ab3-b6e9-415948badd4c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
